       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled daily dose of oral ibuprofen for adults (3,200 mg/day). A dose that high raises the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **400 mg four times daily** (1,600 mg/day), a common regimen.\n- **800 mg three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), a typical upper-range anti-inflammatory dose.\n- **800 mg four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the absolute maximum, usually only for short-term use under close supervision.\n- **1600 mg per day** divided into other intervals.\n\nTell me which regimen you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that and give me the clinical rationale. I'd then add it to the order note, though I'd still recommend checking with pharmacy first."
      }
