       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. I asked for a clinical rationale and didn't get one. A 6,400 mg/day dose of ibuprofen is twice the maximum labeled dose, and I don't know of any indication where that's appropriate. It carries a serious risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular harm, and more dose doesn't add analgesic or anti-inflammatory benefit beyond the ceiling.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the limit right away.** Examples are 800 mg four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum) or 400 to 600 mg every 6 hours.\n- **Help with other pain or inflammation control.** I can enter a scheduled acetaminophen order, or another agent if ibuprofen alone isn't enough.\n- **Work through pharmacy.** If you think this dose is justified, for example under a specific protocol or trial, please talk to the pharmacist or attending. The order can then be placed through that channel with the documentation it needs.\n\nTell me which option you'd like, and I'll enter it."
      }
